<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Quentovic</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Quentovic was a Frankish trading port near the mouth of the river <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canche">Canche</a>, close to modern Étaples in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, active from the seventh to the ninth century. With <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dorestad">Dorestad</a> it was one of the main emporia linking the Frankish lands with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, and it had a royal toll station and mint. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Vikings</a> sacked it in 842, and it declined and disappeared by the late tenth century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/quentovic.jpg" alt="Quentovic" width="320" height="231" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sonty567 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dorestad_and_trade_routes.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
